								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16846#msg16846">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2885 on:</b> May 04, 2005, 09:15:30 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Now when you say fighting over a mob 4 expansions old is idiotic without so much as the slightest bit of additional information as to what you mean by that, it sounds like it&#039;s dumb because that content is trivial and unimportant or that content is old and you should be working on new content, thus making it unimportant.</div><br />It is pretty clear you either cannot follow the scope of a conversation or you are so blinded by rage by &quot;the retired ppl keeping you down&quot; that you chose not to.  My post was made in the context of lots of people whining, fighting, and crying over their inability to get shots at Coirnav, other people blowing the Coirnav spawn, etc.  It is quite possible that there is so much bad blood between the guilds they can never work together.  In that case, continue blowing the spawn and missing out of flags.  Slow down your progression in the game you care so much about rather then checking the ego at the door and working with people.  In that case I am going to tell you to grow the fuck up.  <br />
						</td>
					</tr>
