								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Don&#039;t bash those who call it like it is, and then try to turn it around on them telling them that they don&#039;t play etc etc etc so thier opinions don&#039;t count. Let&#039;s get back to the topic that was brought up.</div><br />But its so easy to use the old &quot;You don&#039;t play anymore, so nobody cares about your opinion, so quit posting here!&quot;&nbsp; Its kind of like when a little kid is cornered in an argument, he responds &quot;Oh yeah, well you&#039;re stupid!&quot;&nbsp; Its an easy out . . . .<br /><br />Oh, and I still think blowing a spawn by killing the trigger when you are fully aware your guild doesn&#039;t have the numbers to kill the actual boss, solely to prevent another guild who DOES have the numbers online and is heading for it from getting it (IL vs. UoP with Coir; or Forsaken and Cursed Cycle with Hegemony/UoP), is different from a guild that simply beats another guild to the boss mob and kills it (UoP v. Hegemony).<br /><br />But I only log in once every 1-2 months is all now, so what do I know . . . .
